Add a TurboSHAKE option

Add a parameter-set option to use TurboSHAKE (RFC 9861) instead of SHAKE for all hashing that
depends on the parameter set: Fiat-Shamir, VOLECommit (the hash of the leaf commitments and the
CRT VOLE masks) and grinding. TurboSHAKE is SHAKE with Keccak-p[1600] reduced from 24 to 12
rounds; we use its default domain separation byte, 0x1F, which matches SHAKE's padding. The default
is SHAKE, so the FAEST parameter sets are unchanged; TurboSHAKE is not compatible with FAEST.

hash_state and hash_state_x4 take the XOF in init(), defaulting to SHAKE. Code that depends on a
parameter set passes P::xof_v. The SHAKE-based PRG and leaf hash (leaf_hash::shake, also used for
the stat-binding leaf hash IV) always use SHAKE.

Build XKCP's TurboSHAKE for the 1-way hash, and instantiate the x4 sponge with
Keccak-p[1600, 12]x4 for the 4-way hash. Also patch XKCP to use the SHA3 instructions for
Keccak-p[1600, 12]x2 on ARMv8A, which fallback-on2 uses for Keccak-p[1600, 12]x4.

TODO(cjpatton) Propose this change to faest-arch-opt authors.

